{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_page", "label": "CBOR-Serializer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_cborserializer", "label": "CborSerializer (RFC 8949)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Interne, abh\u00e4ngigkeitsfreie Implementierung; jeder RFC-8949-konforme Decoder liest die Kodierung. Sinnvoll bei Bin\u00e4rdaten, abgerechneter Cluster-Bandbreite, gr\u00f6\u00dfenskalierenden Storage-Kosten oder Millionen kleiner Nachrichten."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_size_comparison", "label": "Gr\u00f6\u00dfenvergleich JSON gegen CBOR", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Typisch 20-40 % kleiner; die gr\u00f6\u00dften Ersparnisse bei Bin\u00e4rdaten (kein base64-Overhead) und wiederholten Feldnamen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_rich_type_parity", "label": "Typ-Parit\u00e4t zwischen JSON und CBOR", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine gemeinsame Test-Suite stellt sicher, dass beide sich bei jedem Typ einig sind. Das war nicht immer so: CborSerializer hat Map, Set und die beiden bidirektionalen Collections fr\u00fcher still zu einem leeren {} plattgemacht (#1036)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_undefined_native", "label": "CBOR tr\u00e4gt undefined nativ (Simple Value 23)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JsonSerializer lehnt undefined rundheraus ab \u2014 CBOR ist hier der gro\u00dfz\u00fcgigere der beiden."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_little_endian_typed_arrays", "label": "Typed Arrays au\u00dfer Uint8Array reisen little-endian", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jede unterst\u00fctzte Runtime ist little-endian; nur relevant, wenn die Bytes selbst an einen Big-Endian-Peer weitergegeben werden."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_setdefault_scope", "label": "setDefault \u00e4ndert nur den Extension-Default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Es r\u00fcstet CBOR nicht auf den Cluster-Wire oder die Persistenz-Stores um: beide schreiben den getaggten JSON-Tree und ziehen die Registry nicht heran. Der unterst\u00fctzte Weg in einen Store ist dessen withSerializer(...); f\u00fcr den Wire gibt es das noch nicht (#450)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_reader_needs_same_serializer", "label": "Jeder Leser eines Stores braucht denselben Serializer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine \u00fcber withSerializer geschriebene Row nennt die Serializer-ID, die sie braucht, und decodePayload wirft statt zu raten; Cross-Node-tells sind nicht betroffen, weil der Wire den getaggten Tree rahmt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_float_precision", "label": "Float-Pr\u00e4zision (IEEE 754)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Beide Formate haben das Problem, bei CBOR ist es sichtbarer, weil die Bytes exakt sind; f\u00fcr Geldbetr\u00e4ge Strings oder Integer-Cent nehmen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_not_human_debuggable", "label": "CBOR ist nicht menschenlesbar debugbar", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Debugging braucht CBOR-Tools; die Wahl gilt pro Store und pro Aufruf, ein CBOR-Journal kann also neben einem JSON-Snapshot-Store stehen \u2014 der Cluster-Wire geh\u00f6rt nicht zu den Wahlm\u00f6glichkeiten."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_cborserializer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_serializer_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_cborserializer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_json_jsonserializer", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_rich_type_parity", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_json_type_tags", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_setdefault_scope", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_registry_not_consulted", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_reader_needs_same_serializer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_serialized_framing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_cborserializer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_withserializer_store", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_size_comparison", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_cbor_cborserializer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/cbor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}